<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Joko Widodo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1961–</span> · Also known as Jokowi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Joko Widodo, known as Jokowi, is an Indonesian politician who served as president from 2014 to 2024. A furniture exporter from Surakarta, he became mayor of that city and governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jakarta">Jakarta</a> before winning the presidency as the first leader from outside the political and military elite. His two terms were marked by heavy investment in roads, ports and dams, the export ban on raw nickel ore and the start of the new capital, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nusantara">Nusantara</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/joko-widodo.jpg" alt="Joko Widodo" width="320" height="385" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ministry of State Secretariat of the Republic of Indonesia (Kementerian Sekretariat Negara Republik Indonesia) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Joko_Widodo_2019_official_portrait.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
